            <ArticleTitle>Epidural steroid injection: a procedure ideally performed with fluoroscopic control.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>554-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Epidural injection of steroid and local anesthesia can be used to treat low back pain. The injection is best performed with fluoroscopic control, with needle placement documented by means of a limited epidurogram. The technique was used in 116 patients; there were only three failures (2.5%) and one complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
